     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording the confirmation."
      }
     ],
